  "about": {
    "headline": "Part engineer, part illustrator, full-time tinkerer.",
    "introduction": "Hi, I'm Alex. I like building things that make people smile the first time they use them — and still work perfectly the hundredth time.",
    "biography": "I grew up drawing comics and taking apart old radios, so it's no surprise I ended up somewhere between design and engineering. I started out building accessible health software, moved into creative agencies to learn motion and storytelling, and now spend most of my time designing AI products that feel friendly rather than intimidating.",
    "background": "BSc in Computer Science from a fictional university, plus a stubborn self-taught streak in illustration and animation. I've worked with startups, studios and cultural institutions across Europe.",
